---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Panel from "@/components/Panel.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config";

const CONTACT = "monkeyproofdev@gmail.com";
const UPDATED = new Date("2026-11-22");
const updatedLabel = UPDATED.toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
  day: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
});
const audioOn = SITE.introAudio.enabled && SITE.introAudio.src.startsWith("http");
const audioHost = audioOn ? new URL(SITE.introAudio.src).hostname : "";
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy | ${SITE.title}`}
  description="What MonkeyProof collects about you (almost nothing) and why."
>
  <Panel class="privacy-panel">
    <article class="privacy">
      <header class="privacy__header">
        <h1 class="page-heading">Privacy</h1>
        <p class="page-lede">
          Short version: no cookies, no analytics, no ads, no tracking pixels. The monkeys don't know
          who you are, and they'd like to keep it that way.
        </p>
        <p class="privacy__updated">Last updated: <time datetime={UPDATED.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>{updatedLabel}</time></p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          This blog is a personal, non-commercial site run by {SITE.author}, who is the data controller
          for the little personal data described below. Questions or requests go to
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What gets collected</h2>
        <h3>Server logs</h3>
        <p>
          Like almost every web server, the one serving this site writes a technical log line for each
          request: IP address, date and time, the page or file requested, the response status, the
          referring page, and your browser's user agent. These logs exist to keep the site running and
          secure (spotting errors, abuse, and attacks). They are not used to profile anyone, not
          combined with other data, and not shared, except where the law requires it. They are kept
          only as long as needed for that purpose and then deleted.
        </p>
        <p>
          The legal basis is legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR): a website can't be operated
          safely without them.
        </p>

        <h3>Your preferences, on your device</h3>
        <p>
          Your chosen theme, wallpaper, and focus mode are saved in your browser's
          <code>localStorage</code> (keys <code>mp.theme</code>, <code>mp.wallpaper</code>,
          <code>mp.focus</code>). They never leave your device and are never sent to a server. You can
          clear them at any time from your browser settings. When you jump to or from
          <a href={SITE.daveos.url}>{SITE.daveos.label}</a>, the theme and wallpaper travel along in the
          link (<code>?theme=&amp;wallpaper=</code>) so both sites look the same. That's all they do.
        </p>

        <h3>Search</h3>
        <p>
          Search runs entirely in your browser against a static index shipped with the site. What you
          type is not sent anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2>What doesn't happen</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No cookies, so no cookie banner.</li>
          <li>No analytics, no ad networks, no tracking or fingerprinting scripts.</li>
          <li>No third-party fonts, CDNs, or embeds: everything is served from this domain.</li>
          <li>No comments, accounts, newsletter, or forms. Nothing you could type in gets stored.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Third parties, only when you choose</h2>
        <p>
          Share buttons and social links (GitHub, LinkedIn, X, Facebook, WhatsApp) are plain links. Nothing
          is loaded from those services until you click one. Once you're on their site, their privacy
          policies apply.
        </p>
        {
          audioOn && (
            <p>
              The lofi radio player streams audio from <code>{audioHost}</code>. Your browser only
              connects to it after you press play, and that provider will then see your IP address like
              any server you connect to.
            </p>
          )
        }
        <p>
          If you write to me by email, I'll use your address and message only to reply, and I won't
          pass them on to anyone.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you can ask for access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data,
          object to its processing, or ask to restrict it. Write to
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. You can also complain to your data protection
          authority. In Italy, that's the
          <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/" rel="noopener">Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If anything here changes (say, if I ever add analytics), this page will say so first and the
          date at the top will move.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Panel>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-panel {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .privacy {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .privacy__header {
    padding-bottom: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin-bottom: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .privacy__updated {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
</style>
